    ("Crab apple", "Malus sylvestris", "fruit", "Astringe and stabilize", "cool", "Sour, Sweet", "Liver, Spleen, Stomach", ["Digestive support", "Thirst", "Loose stool", "Food stagnation"], "Crab apple is sour-sweet and cooling, useful as a local astringent digestive fruit when cooked.", "Usually cooked. Use caution with reflux, diarrhea, or high sugar preserves.", "hardy_outdoors", "Crab apples are hardy UK trees and valuable for wildlife and pollination.", "A local sour apple for astringent and digestion-support notes.", "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Crab%20apples.jpg"),
    ("Greengage", "Prunus domestica subsp. italica", "fruit", "Tonify deficiency", "cool", "Sweet, Sour", "Stomach, Large Intestine", ["Dryness", "Constipation", "Thirst", "Mild deficiency"], "Greengage is a sweet-sour plum type, best mapped as cooling and fluid-supporting with mild bowel-moistening action.", "Use caution with diarrhea, fructose intolerance, or blood sugar management.", "hardy_outdoors", "Greengages can grow outdoors in warmer UK sites, with crop reliability helped by shelter and pollination.", "A sweet plum relative for cooling moistening food-therapy comparisons.", "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Greengage.jpg"),
