    ("Beeswax", "Cera alba", "other_food", "Culinary support", "neutral", "Sweet", "Lung, Spleen, Skin", ["Dryness", "Skin irritation", "Culinary support"], "Beeswax is mainly a preparation base, coating, or salve ingredient rather than a primary food-therapy item; medicinal context is mostly topical or formulation-related.", "Avoid with bee product allergy. Use only food/cosmetic-grade wax as appropriate and avoid ingesting non-food wax preparations.", "not_practical", "Beeswax is produced by honey bees and recovered from comb; beekeeping requires training, equipment, and local permission.", "A hive product used as a base or stabiliser for balms, salves, coatings, and some traditional preparations.", "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Honey_comb.jpg"),
