    ("Bee pollen", "Bee pollen", "other_food", "Tonify deficiency", "neutral", "Sweet", "Spleen, Lung, Liver", ["Fatigue", "Mild deficiency", "Dryness", "Seasonal sensitivity"], "Bee pollen is a concentrated bee-collected pollen product used as a food supplement; traditional framing is best kept gentle and constitution-dependent.", "Avoid with pollen or bee product allergy, asthma, pregnancy unless supervised, anticoagulants, or complex medication schedules. Allergic reactions can be serious.", "not_practical", "Bee pollen is collected by bees from flowering plants and trapped by beekeepers; composition varies by season and forage.", "A hive-derived food supplement for cautious tonic and seasonal-support comparisons.", "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/Apis_mellifera_-_Melilotus_albus_-_Keila.jpg"),
